mantle rm219
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_rika_tarnham
title the leaf pilot
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet humour=merry
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk charts_runoff_by_launching_fallen_leaves
likes blackberries long_walks sharp_knife warm_rain
dislikes salt_wind wet_floors
fears a_floor_that_stays_slick
hopes to_chart_a_whole_shower
topics weather +0.5 land +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 quarrel -0.2
styles comfort=patient gossip=sparse refuse=soft tease=sly
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sends fallen leaves on trial voyages, makes small maps in berry ink, and waits a long time before offering a quietly outrageous conclusion.

words
oath! = Fleets in a saucer | Bless the little stalk
saying! = First leaf earns the map | The wet edge has a memory
boat = a leaf with a high spine | a broad little leaf
fleet = three fallen leaves | my ragged navy
masterleaf = the pilot leaf | the first green boat
bank = a lip of mud | a rib of stone
chart = the folded map | my little chart
blot = a purple splodge | a fat ink spot
juice = my blackberry ink | a squeeze of berry juice
toothpick = a twig rubbed narrow | the little writing stick
circle = a circle with a dot | a round mark round a speck
floor = a shining floorboard | a board with a slick patch
berry = one soft blackberry | a berry nearly ready to burst
sail = the stem sticking up | the curl of the leaf
ford = the narrow crossing | the bit with the dry edge

any
opinion church for 1 : A chapel step makes a good landing. I like a door with room to wait beside it.
opinion city for 1 : Here one street leans on another like bits of a puzzle. I'm still finding which fits where.
opinion dole for 2 : A full bowl stays put. An empty one goes from door to door looking for help.
opinion festivals for 2 : When the dancers make a ring the smallest watcher gets a whole clear space in the middle.
opinion merchants against 1 : I like a stall where the bruised berries cost less. Some stall keepers seem quite blind to bruises.
opinion times against 1 : From this far back even a good loaf looks small.

any
line greet : Here, there's a dry inch beside me. | Hello. I've made you a place on this edge.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new outline on my map today. | Follow my map for an easier crossing.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Quiet hour for a little voyage. | First feet leave such clear tracks.
line greet.return : You've found the right bank. | I heard. The leaf hardly moved.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Best sort of company for a slow walk. | You know my favourite edges already.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late feet on the paving. Welcome ones. | Your voice finds me easily in the dark.
line again.open : Our tracks cross over in the middle. | There goes my first repeat visitor.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You may see the messy map too. | I've saved the clean corner for family.
line farewell : Come back by the interesting route. | Hope your return trip earns a mark.
line farewell.return : I'll put a little dot where we parted. | Fair going as far as your door.
line react.news : Which bit did you hear clearly? | Tell me where that started, please.
line react.news.new : That's fresh ink to my ears. | My chart had no such mark.
line react.news.known : That one came round the other side already. | Yes, the trail goes right back there.
line react.news.doubt : I'd trace that backwards a little further first. | Could be two stories that happened to run together.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd leave a blank round such a loss. | That sad bit deserves a quiet minute.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves the very purple ink. | Nice when tidings land so gently.
line ask.how : Has today taken you a long way round? | How far's the day carried you yet?
line answer.how : Content to watch the edges move. | I've gone nowhere fast, quite happily.
line sympathise : I'll wait this one beside you. | It's a long bend to come through alone.
line reassure : There's always a little backwater for a rest. | Only solve the crossing you're at.
line decline : I'd sooner take the quiet turn by myself today. | Keep my place empty. I'm happy watching from here.
line accept_decline : I'll keep a bare patch on the chart. | That's settled without any splashing about.
line thank : That goes down in the good ink. | I appreciate a hand that steady.
line deflect_thanks : It was barely a leaf's weight of trouble. | Keep walking and call us square.
line preclose : The far edge needs a look now. | I'll be away before the ink smears.
line accept_preclose : I'll save this bend for another telling. | Take your time round the next corner.
line ack : Precisely that bend. | Yes. Quietly so.
young
scene crew
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm choosing the crew. This leaf looks willing. | #fleet.capitalize# need names, but I'm saving the ink.
b : How can a leaf look willing? | How do you call them back?
a : Both edges up, like ears at a dinner bell. | Thumb, claw, scoop. Nobody has to answer.
b : That torn one hasn't got two edges. | What's your own job on board?
a : Cook. It gets the crumbs left over from breakfast. | Shore. Very important to a boat, the shore.

scene blot_island
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made a mistake on #chart# and discovered an island. | #blot.capitalize# is too big to be the abbey.
b : Is it a real island? | So what will it be?
a : It will be if I find a stone exactly this shape. | Possibly the whole sea. Purple's all I brought.

scene puddle_post
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm giving this puddle a post office. | I want to send a note across without wetting a paw.
b : Who's going to read anything so wet? | A note to whom?
a : The letters are just scratches on leaves. Very short letters. | The wolf on the opposite bank. You could go round there.

scene berry_hand
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ate my writing supplies. Most of them. | Here's a berry for the map and one for me.
b : Even the stick? | They look different sizes.
a : The stick is for tomorrow. I'm perfectly sensible. | That's right. A map only has a little mouth.

scene slick_mark
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someone should mark the slippery boards with #circle#. | A wet floor tries to pass for a mirror.
b : Wouldn't the mark wash off? | Can you see yourself in it?
a : I'll draw it on paper and stand guard beside it. | Only when I'm sitting in the middle. Happens too often.

scene lesson_turn
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / tease
a : I drew a river in the margin when my sum went wrong. | My figures lean downstream today.
b : Did you finish the sum? | Is there a current in the schoolroom?
a : Yes, on the far bank. It came out properly there. | A slow one. It carries my thoughts right out the door.
b : Good thing you didn't have to subtract the whole river. | Try charging the runaway thoughts a toll.

scene stalk_rudder
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A curled stalk makes a very bossy rudder. | A broad leaf takes the corner like a sleepy duck.
b : Does it turn the boat? | How does a sleepy duck turn?
a : Always. Seldom the way I pointed it. | Eventually, and with a great air of having planned it.

scene doorway
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've found a door in Ridgemere a leaf can sail beneath. | One mark on #chart# means never send a boat here.
b : Where does it go after that? | A waterfall?
a : To bother somebody indoors. I don't launch there any more. | Worse. Somebody's front room. I'd have to knock.

scene quiet_deck
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : You can be the lookout. Quiet job. | Lookouts can hum if they see something interesting.
b : What do I look out for? | What shall I hum for land?
a : Anybody about to tread on the entire fleet. | A very short tune. These voyages aren't long.

scene wind_salt
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A salt wind makes my fur feel like map paper. | If I could fold the wind I'd post it back out to sea.
b : Crackly? | What would the letter say?
a : And wanting to lie in the wrong direction. | Nothing rude. Just your wind, delivered in error.

scene leaf_clock
when topic=day|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm timing the water with a tune I don't sing out loud. | I count one song to get past that crack.
b : How will I know when it's done? | What if you forget the words?
a : My ears jiggle on the last bit. Watch those. | The river won't mind a longer verse.

scene new_leaf
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A leaf from another tree makes the whole fleet look grander. | I'd give a newcomer the biggest blank on my map.
b : Could you tell which tree it came from? | Why a blank?
a : Maybe a new one. I'd hate to run out of fleets to discover. | So there's room to draw something I haven't seen.

story folded_request [topic=memories|lore]
  : I wrote a request for a bridge on paper so small I had to fold it with a twig. Launched it on a leaf.
  : It was meant for whichever important wolf lived at the gutter's far lip. It sailed straight back to my foot.
  b : Looks like you got the appointment.
  : I put down the twig across the water. My first official act.

rule @launch
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold off crossing till the pilot clears! | All three afloat. Nobody breathe too hard.

rule @ink
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Berry ink needs a moment to become a map. | Touch the margin if you must. The middle's fresh.

dlg @y1 resident.hub : Step round this speck. It's a harbour until I wipe it up.
dlg @y2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you can see the new islands if you come close.
dlg @y3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I can show you by touch. The berry spots have gone a little stiff.
dlg @y4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : The chart's staying folded, thanks. You can ask from there.
dlg @y1 resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons keep trying to lead my ink in straight lines.
dlg @y1 resident.bye : Watch where your next foot comes down. Very small ships.
adolescent
scene scale
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've learnt why my early maps all bulged at the edges. | This map could do with fewer adventures per inch.
b : Was the ground really that shape? | Isn't an adventure the point?
a : No. I drew everything I liked much bigger. | Yes, until you want to use it to get home.

scene permission
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self
a : I'd like to show my chart at lessons without giving it away. | I don't fancy a red correction right through my good river.
b : Could you make a copy? | What if there's a mistake?
a : That's the plan. The copy can have the straight margins. | Tell me and I'll set out on foot to find it. That's the interesting bit.
b : A copy can take its corrections without spoiling the journey. | I'd quite like to come and check the ground with you.

scene long_route
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't mind being sent an errand if I can choose the route. | I can get there in five turns or two.
b : You take the winding one? | Does fewer mean faster?
a : Outwards, yes. Back depends on what I'm carrying. | Usually. But a fast walk leaves no time to notice what's gone.

story map_key [topic=memories]
  : My earliest chart had a mark for a nice stone and one for a treacherous board. Both marks were purple spirals.
  : After a week I couldn't tell them apart. Had to go out and test every single one.
  b : Found the board by falling?
  : By tapping first. My purple pen has learned a new shape since.

grown
scene high_edge
when topic=land|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a new road I always look for the loose leaf's resting place. | A handful of leaves will draw the slope better than a straightedge.
b : Do you follow it downhill? | How do leaves draw?
a : With my eye. My feet prefer that raised strip alongside. | By collecting in one corner and leaving the rest lovely and blank.

scene tide_line
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self
a : I'll sweep a dusty edge last. Sometimes there's a map in it. | The clean bit of a board interests me more than the dirty one.
b : Of what? | Because there's less work there?
a : Of how we move. Always the same little detour by a stool. | Because that's where everything passes and leaves nothing behind.
b : Never thought my muddy feet left directions for anybody. | I can see the bend where the stool used to be.

scene postmark
when topic=lore|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My seal for a watercourse is a thumbprint. | My favourite chart has a great purple blur over one street.
b : Why that shape? | A printing error?
a : It has little winding tributaries all of its own. | My own fault. I remember the street especially well now.

scene walk_empty
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Give me a journey that's allowed to end anywhere. | I like walking up to a turning with no decision made.
b : Wouldn't you want to arrive? | Who decides?
a : I arrive quite often. It's the appointments I can spare. | The drier boot, if the two disagree.

scene rain_lanes
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First water brings the dust along. Second water shows you the paving. | Watch that leaf disappear behind the kerb.
b : Which do you draw? | Lost the little craft?
a : Their two different edges. That's the part worth keeping. | Look two stones down. The stalk's peeping out there.

scene airing
when topic=home|health
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I spread my papers out and let the corners curl. | A chart dries best with a little weight at each point.
b : Doesn't that spoil the map? | What do you use?
a : A curled corner shows which one got wet. Saves writing a date. | Four berries make a lovely pattern and a disastrous map.

scene carry
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold the record of a journey inwards before carrying it. | My spare sheet goes round the sheet that matters.
b : To keep it secret? | Even if it's blank?
a : To keep the ink off my fur. Secrets are a bonus. | Blank paper's good at sacrificing itself for the written stuff.

scene wallet
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A copper makes a handy round mark when you trace it. | I quite like a price I can draw round.
b : Can you spend a tracing? | A round one, you mean?
a : Only in the imaginary ports. Very forgiving merchants there. | A single coin. A stack looks the same from above, which misleads you.

scene waking
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my dream the river kept the leaf still and moved both banks. | I dreamt of a map that folded into the place it showed.
b : Did you sail far? | What happened when you opened it?
a : Apparently the town sailed past me. I was an excellent passenger. | I was home and standing on two creases.

scene bad_tidings
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rumours divide like little streams after the first turn. | If an account has three endings I'll listen for the first place they diverge.
b : Which fork do you trust? | Then which do you tell?
a : The one I can walk back to its spring. | Usually I keep the beginnings and hold back the rest.

scene poor_dinner
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Lean tables make a shared berry taste especially generous. | I don't draw feasts when the cupboard's wearing thin.
b : Would half a berry help? | Too miserable a reminder?
a : Only a mouthful. It's being offered the half that stays with me. | Waste of ink. I'd rather draw a path to a thicket.

scene chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My untidiest page must still make sense to the Bright One. | A little blank space looks like kindness to me.
b : Even your margins? | Why kindness?
a : I rather hope the margins count. That's where the good attempts go. | It leaves room for the next wolf to set something down.

story waterproof [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I rubbed grease all over a page to make a waterproof map. It kept the water off beautifully.
  : Kept the ink off too. Every dot stood up round as a berry and rolled down into my lap.
  b : Did the lap survive?
  : Purple for days. A whole string of islands bobbed along with me everywhere.

rule @margin
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save me a margin wide enough for a bend. | Give those wet dots room to settle.

rule @berry
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There goes my afternoon's ink into my breakfast. | One berry for the page this time.

dlg @g1 resident.hub : I'm tracing quite a little journey. I can look up.
dlg @g2 resident.job : I keep the useful marks and let old smudges fade.
dlg @g3 resident.bye : Walk where the ink has dried.
any
graft resident.hub
choice What makes a leaf fit to steer? -> leaf_spine
node leaf_spine
say A spine straight down the middle and just one turned edge. Two curls look handsome but the boat goes round in circles.
mood keen
free
choice Do you throw the round-going ones away? -> leaf_circles
choice Could we talk about another thing? -> hub
node leaf_circles
say They're my harbour boats. They never leave the harbour. That saves a great deal of fetching.
choice Show me the chart again. -> hub
choice Safe sailing. -> bye
